# sketch Connecting an agent
# The onboarding design (docs/plan-onboarding.md) without its positions: the
# text whose group regions crossed each other, laid out fresh. The
# dashboard's arrow back to the connect page closes a cycle, which the
# layering sets aside (docs/format.md, Layout, step 2).
direction: right
agents: box "/connect page\npick your client" solid tag "Web"
claude: box "Claude\none add, five surfaces" tint tag "Client"
editors: box "Cursor · VS Code · goose\ninstall buttons" tint tag "Client"
clis: box "Codex · Gemini · OpenCode\ncopy a command" tint tag "Client"
other: box "ChatGPT · Zed · JetBrains\npaste the address" tag "Client"
mcp: box "ttmi MCP server\n/mcp, AuthKit sign-in" solid tag "Server"
status: box "Connected?\ndashboard banner, page status" tint tag "Web"
plugin: box "ttmi plugin\nskill + connector" tint tag "Repo"
listings: box "MCP registry\nAnthropic directory" tag "After launch"
links: note tag "Verified" width 460
  ## Install links

  ```text
  cursor://anysphere.cursor-deeplink/mcp/install
    ?name=ttmi&config=<base64 {"url":"https://ttmi.ai/mcp"}>
  https://vscode.dev/redirect/mcp/install
    ?name=ttmi&config=<urlencoded {name,type:"http",url}>
  goose://extension?type=streamable_http
    &url=https://ttmi.ai/mcp&id=ttmi&name=ttmi
  ```
signal: note tag "Data model" width 420
  ## users/{uid}.agent

  ```ts
  type Agent = { client: string; lastSeenAt: string };
  // { client: "Claude Code", lastSeenAt: "…T09:12:00Z" }
  ```

  Stamped by the server on each MCP call. Unset: the dashboard shows a banner that leads to /connect. Set: client and time.
layout: note tag "Repo" width 460
  ## Plugin layout

  ```text
  .claude-plugin/marketplace.json    -> ./plugins/ttmi
  plugins/ttmi/.claude-plugin/plugin.json
  plugins/ttmi/.mcp.json             { type: http, url }
  plugins/ttmi/skills/ttmi/SKILL.md  (moved from skill/)
  ```

  ```text
  claude plugin install ttmi --marketplace christianalfoni/ttmi
  ```
site: group "ttmi.ai" of agents, status, mcp
clients: group "Agent clients" of claude, editors, clis, other
repo: group "GitHub repo" of plugin, layout
agents -> claude "open Connectors"
agents -> editors "one click"
agents -> clis "copy command"
agents -> other "copy address"
claude -> mcp "sign in, call tools"
editors -> mcp "sign in, call tools"
clis -> mcp "sign in, call tools"
other -> mcp "sign in, call tools"
mcp -> status "stamps agent"
status -> agents "banner leads here"
plugin -> claude "skill + connector"
plugin -> listings "submit"
links -> editors
signal -> status
layout -> plugin

step: agents claude editors clis other
  The Agents page becomes Connect: a client picker instead of a wall of cards.

step: mcp status signal
  Every path ends at the same sign-in and the same server, which stamps the user.
